<title>USA: Dow Corning provides $2.95 billion to settle implant suits.</title>
<headline>Dow Corning provides $2.95 billion to settle implant suits.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dow Corning Corp. has agreed to provide about $2.95 billion to settle thousands of silicon breast implant lawsuits under a plan to emerge from Chapter 11 bankruptcy protection, the company and its creditors said Friday.</p>
<p>The joint reorganization plan involves setting up a $1.75 billion trust to resolve and pay all product liability claims by women who charge that Dow Corning's silicon implants caused injury or disease. Another $1.2 billion will be provided to compensate commercial claims, they said.</p>
</text>
